  "schema": "limina.visual-design-contract/v1",
  "id": "furniture/dining-table/v1",
  "subjectKind": "furniture",
  "intendedFunction": "A compact four-place oak dining and work table for the cottage hall, stable on an uneven-looking timber floor while preserving knee room, chair approaches, and circulation inside the approved I1 envelope.",
  "prompt": "Author a cohesive late-medieval oak trestle dining table from a dimensioned human-use section. Fit the exact 1400 by 800 by 780 mm I1 envelope. Use a substantial eased plank top, two inset trestle frames with broad floor feet, a low longitudinal stretcher secured by visibly plausible wedged through-tenons, and restrained chamfering. Derive every member from one load path: top into trestles, trestles into feet, and trestles tied by the stretcher. Preserve four-chair knee clearance, authored floor contact, centered local origin, exposed end grain at joints, and longitudinal grain on the top. Ornament must remain subordinate to construction.",
